    <sectiondef kind="define">
      <memberdef kind="define" id="group__scl__feature__reflection_1ga04334714025d2e271f8c953464c5382d" prot="public" static="no">
        <name>SCL_REFLECT_TYPE</name>
        <param><defname>type</defname></param>
        <param><defname>executor</defname></param>
        <initializer>    using S_c_L_type_ = type;            \
    using S_c_L_executor_type_ = executor;</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Declares the wrapper and executor types for use by <computeroutput>SCL_REFLECT_METHOD</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Must appear inside the class body <bold>before</bold> any <computeroutput>SCL_REFLECT_METHOD</computeroutput> invocations.</para>
<para>A specialization of <computeroutput><ref refid="structscl_1_1feature_1_1executor__trait" kindref="compound">scl::feature::executor_trait</ref></computeroutput> must also be provided for <computeroutput>type</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="group__scl__feature__reflection_1ga04334714025d2e271f8c953464c5382d" kindref="member">SCL_REFLECT_TYPE</ref>(MyWrapper,<sp/>MyExecutor);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</simplesect>
